/-!
# R4: Minkowski Cartesian ↔ spherical — the actual coordinate map on a chart

Chart `domChart = {r > 0, 0 < θ < π, 0 < φ < 2π}` ⊆ `domSph`. The map
`toCart (t, r, θ, φ) = (t, r sin θ cos φ, r sin θ sin φ, r cos θ)` is a `C^∞` bijection of
`domChart` onto `imgCart = ℝ⁴ ∖ {y = 0, x ≥ 0}` (the closed half-plane slit, which contains the
`z`-axis), with `C^∞` inverse `fromCart`. The Jacobian `jac` has genuine-derivative entries,
`det jac = r² sin θ`, and the pull-back identity `jacᵀ · η · jac = gSph` holds on the chart.
`φ ~ φ + 2π` is not formalised; this is one chart.
-/

